{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Flow step debugger P1 core (spec: dev/_ASSETS/docs/flow-language.md 1.5.4). step(state, pick) -> {status, state, event, ready, default, ended}: advances a flow ONE step and emits one event (enter, seed, deliver, sync, eval, next, terminate, fail, finish, done, stall, error). Pure over plain ndata: start with state = {body: the flow's root Case JSON, args}, then pass back the returned state; the graph is never mutated and the frame is copied per step. pick = {} takes the DEFAULT pick (flowlang's sweep order, so continuing with {} gives the same run as Code::execute); {kind: wire|sync|op, index} picks a READY item - anything else is refused with status err and the state unchanged. ready lists the ready items ({kind:auto} at enter/seed/close, {kind:effect} when a fired rule's effect is next). Honors Case.syncs. One frame: local and command ops (flow callees in any library, rust/python) evaluate in a single eval step, list/loop ops as one eval with iters. An op runs once - a second delivery is reported as I-1 instead of re-running it. I-4 gives an error event and a stuck case a stall event: no panic, no hang (nested evaluation budget 100000 steps, depth 64).","import":"use flowlang::primitives::Primitive;\nuse flowlang::command::Command;\nuse flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse ndata::data::Data;\nuse std::panic;","params":[{"name":"state","type":"JSONObject"},{"name":"pick","type":"JSONObject"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"kwjhgp1a16a026788s1c8","readers":[],"time":1792782653214,"username":"system","writers":[]}